		(property "Manufacturer" "Epson"
			(at 269.24 36.83 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "Epson FC-135 32.768 kHz, CL = 6 pF. CHANGED from C32346 (Q13FC13500004, CL 12.5 pF), which was BOUGHT ON PRICE AND NEVER CHECKED AGAINST THE SoC. D-3 deletes the external load capacitors, so the whole load is the nRF54L's on-die caps, and Nordic's own numbers refuse 12.5 pF twice over. Datasheet 4503_018 v1.0 (Sept 2025) Sec 5.5.2: OSCILLATORS.XOSC32KI.INTCAP holds 3-18 pF in 0.65 pF steps, and with internal caps CL = (C_INT + C_pcb)/2, so the highest CL reachable is about (18+2)/2 = 10 pF - 12.5 pF needs C_INT ~= 23 pF, 5 pF above the hardware maximum. Sec 11.9.2 refuses it again at the part level: CL_LFXO min 6 pF, MAX 9 pF, which holds whether the caps are internal or external. Nordic's own reference BOM (Sec 10.3) is a CL 9 pF 2012 crystal with NO external load capacitors. A 12.5 pF crystal here does not start, or starts far off frequency, and the board looks simply dead. OPEN: 6 pF is inside the 6-9 pF window but at its edge; a 9 pF part in this body would centre it. Package still assumed to be the 3215 land pattern and NOT confirmed against Epson's drawing. Still 0.9 mm tall, which X-5's height delta binds."
			(at 269.24 36.83 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Price@1k" "TBC"
			(at 269.24 36.83 0)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
				(hide yes)
			)
		)
		(property "Priced" "2026-09-03"
			(at 269.24 36.83 0)
